course: dictionary
lesson: 9149
title: Snitch or keep safe?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A snitch is someone who tells an adult that another person has done something wrong. Snitch is informal, and it can be unkind, so the meaning often depends on why someone tells. «Telling an adult about a friend's dangerous plan can save a life, and it isn't snitching or grassing (telling tales).» The words around snitch show that telling can be good when someone could get hurt.
explain: Some people call any telling "snitching" to stop others reporting harm. «Some children call any telling "snitching" to stop people reporting harm.» Ask yourself: is the telling to keep someone safe, or only to get someone into trouble? The context clues help you decide.
explain: Snitch has other meanings too. In Harry Potter, the Golden Snitch is a small flying ball in Quidditch. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If "tells an adult" still makes sense, then snitch means telling on someone.
fact: To snitch means to tell an adult that someone has done something wrong, and it is often unkind.
fact: A snitch is a person who tells on others.
fact: To snitch can also mean to steal something small, as in «snitch a biscuit».
fact: Snitch on someone means to tell on them.
fact: «Yabeda» means telltale or snitch, and kids hate being called it.
exercise: «Telling an adult about a friend's dangerous plan can save a life, and it isn't snitching.» Is telling an adult here snitching? | Only if the adult is a teacher | Yes, but only on a Tuesday | Yes, always, whatever the reason | *No, it is telling to keep someone safe
exercise: In Harry Potter, what is the Golden Snitch? | A large, slow animal | A type of cake | A school bell | *A small flying ball in Quidditch
exercise: Yesterday Sam ___ a biscuit from the tin when nobody was looking. Which word fills the gap? | snitches | snitch | snitching | *snitched
test: «Some children call any telling "snitching" to stop people reporting harm.» What does this sentence suggest? | *Some people use the word snitch to stop others telling about harm | Harm is never worth reporting | Telling an adult is always wrong | Children never talk about snitching
test: What does a snitch do? | *Tells an adult about someone who has done something wrong | Hides a ball for a game | Sings a song in the playground | Gives a prize to a friend
exam: Max's friend plans something dangerous, so Max tells his teacher to keep his friend safe. Is Max snitching? | No, because Max stole a biscuit | Yes, because the teacher is an adult | *Not really, telling an adult to keep someone safe is the right thing | Yes, any telling is snitching, so Max is in trouble
